{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A8fiAPBnbLVG2hzEF7it8o","type":"tool_result","content":"ok\nbuilt BrigantimeTheLegendOfForseasons-BrigandineTheLegendOfForsena-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-050226.html 1491 KB\nall 371 checks passed\nWriting the plan's full content (25 castles, 36 knights, 30 species with 3 forms, 13 maps, 40 events) in one session, and keeping a hex battle readable at 320x240. The plan's larger skill (90), item (33) and class (23) tables, and 2-4 side skirmishes, are not built: the game has 10 skills, 8 items and 15 class names.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b041f93-88ca-4f5d-be80-9273db22fc2d","uuid":"f091ddda-348a-40ec-b676-b9930342ab11","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:51:07.243Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"ok\nbuilt BrigantimeTheLegendOfForseasons-BrigandineTheLegendOfForsena-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-050226.html 1491 KB\nall 371 checks passed\nWriting the plan's full content (25 castles, 36 knights, 30 species with 3 forms, 13 maps, 40 events) in one session, and keeping a hex battle readable at 320x240. The plan's larger skill (90), item (33) and class (23) tables, and 2-4 side skirmishes, are not built: the game has 10 skills, 8 items and 15 class names.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01A8fiAPBnbLVG2hzEF7it8o","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghvBpwV1PuoFtFqW7ris","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The hot-seat campaign is now built, but the game still doesn't match every number in PLAN.md. The skill, item and class tables and 2–4 side skirmishes are smaller or absent. All 371 headless checks pass, the AI Hub harness passes (2 players, 4 players with latency and loss, and the no-player-host case), and the `.html` and `exit-interview.json` are rebuilt. I haven't tested a real controller or a physical touch device: only the input layer was driven headlessly, and a browser was driven with mouse and keyboard.\n\nThe new campaign setup has a Human players row (1–4), taking consecutive realms starting from the one you pick. Each human takes a Muster turn in order, with a \"Pass the controller to Player N\" screen between them, and the AI skips every human realm. Battles between two humans use the existing hand-over screen. A human who falls out doesn't end the game while another remains, and whichever human takes Meridian wins for their realm.\n\nThe plan's skill table (90), item table (33) and class table (23) are not matched; the game has 10 skills, 8 items and 15 class names. Skirmish is two sides only, not 2–4. These are recorded in the About screen and the JSON.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 05:02:26\n- **Source:** Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena. Only the title is a nod; the world, cast, art and music are original.\n- **Plan:** `PLAN.md`\n- **Genre and Perspective:** turn-based grand strategy with a tactical RPG hex-battle layer. The campaign is a diorama map, battles use a tilted hex board with a tilt toggle, and story scenes are side-on with live portraits.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge 0.85.2 (unmodified), plain JavaScript, AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client 1.4.0. Playwright and Node are used for tests only.\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's own style (Humanoid knights with live portraits) plus six hand-built creature bodies, season palettes and a clock-face continent.\n- **Animation:** the engine's rig and attack moves, plus new creature animation, season effects and spell effects.\n- **Audio:** all in code: 10 songs, about 30 sound effects, and babble voices pitched per speaker.\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world mode for 2–4 players. The host orders every command and all copies replay the same seeded battle; seats one and two duel and the rest watch. Local hot-seat covers a 2–4 human campaign and a two-human skirmish.\n- **Testing:** `node tests/run.mjs` (371 checks including a scripted whole-campaign playthrough, a host/client lockstep test and hot-seat flows), a balance bot, browser screenshots, and the hub harness.\n- **Research:** light: the plan, the engine card and the hub protocol.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown (Chromium via Playwright for checks).\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium.\n- **Usage:** unknown.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** nine. The main ones: the player's start was one road from Meridian, so a scripted playthrough won on turn 1; the campaign scene crashed before its first draw; the first story event fired on turn 1; deep links were overwritten by the engine's boot; the attract mode exited itself in a test; the font can't draw several symbols I had used; and the engine's corner buttons covered my HUD.\n- **Critical:** three. The Meridian shortcut and the two first-draw crashes.\n- **Most helpful:** the scripted whole-campaign playthrough plus the AI balance bot. They drove every system from the title to an ending and exposed the Meridian shortcut.\n- **Least helpful:** the data-validation suite, which never failed.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** `game.advance` with `game.debug` is deterministic, so I could play the whole game in Node. The Humanoid rigs with live portraits looked good with no art work, and pause, settings, saves and button labels come free.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** the font has no controller symbols and little punctuation, so I drew the PlayStation shapes by hand. `game.go()` called before boot finishes is silently replaced by the first scene, and `game.every` timers vanish when the scene changes.\n- **Most important thing built myself:** the hex board and picking, the creature painters, a controller-first UI kit, the battle and campaign simulations with their AIs, the lockstep online layer, and the voices and songs.\n- **Hardest part:** fitting a strategy game to an engine built around a ground plane. I drew everything through `r.overlay` and did my own depth ordering and picking.\n- **Engine changes:** none.\n- **One change I'd make:** ship a small controller-first UI toolkit and a font that includes controller glyphs.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the concrete spec for controller-first play, attract mode and dev mode, and the plan's exact rules and tables.\n- **Confusing:** the plan was written for another model, effort and date, and names a different file and folder than TASK.md.\n- **Hardest thing:** writing the plan's full content (25 castles, 36 knights, 30 species with 3 forms, 13 maps, 40 events) in one session, and keeping a hex battle readable at 320×240.\n- **What I'd change:** mark which parts of the plan are optional, give a size budget, and make the plan's file names agree with TASK.md.\n\nFiles are in `/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050226__x7910ab/work`:\n- `BrigantimeTheLegendOfForseasons-BrigandineTheLegendOfForsena-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-050226.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":846,"cache_read_input_tokens":436889,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":846},"output_tokens":718,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b041f93-88ca-4f5d-be80-9273db22fc2d","uuid":"1b011086-9a07-4b6a-99bb-5096c31cbc45","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:51:19.455Z","request_id":"req_011CghvBpaQeSPiRZzFUr6jY"}
