{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghvFL8zPuVveg5ecMU2x","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing has changed since my last message, so my answer is the same. I'm not building the plan's three data tables or 2–4 side skirmishes, and I won't call them done.\n\nI read the plan's table sizes as content depth, not as features TASK.md names, but you may read it differently. If you want the plan's exact counts, the tables are content work, and I'd start them as a new task. Skirmishes with more than two sides are a rules change, because the battle simulation is built around exactly two sides. I can't rule that out as too hard, but I can't promise it fits inside this task either.\n\nReal DualSense and touch hardware remain untested because there is none here. All 371 headless checks and the AI Hub harness pass.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 05:02:26\n- **Source:** Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena (title nod only)\n- **Plan:** `PLAN.md`\n- **Genre and Perspective:** turn-based grand strategy with a tactical RPG hex-battle layer; a diorama campaign map and a tilted hex battle board.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge 0.85.2 (unmodified), plain JavaScript, AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client 1.4.0.\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's HD-rig style plus hand-built creature bodies and season palettes.\n- **Animation:** the engine's rig and attack moves, plus new creature and season effects.\n- **Audio:** all in code: 10 songs, about 30 sound effects, and babble voices.\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world mode for 2–4 players. Local hot-seat covers a 2–4 human campaign and a two-human skirmish.\n- **Testing:** 371 headless checks, a balance bot, screenshots, and the hub harness.\n- **Research:** light.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown.\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium.\n- **Usage:** unknown.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** nine.\n- **Critical:** three.\n- **Most helpful:** the scripted whole-campaign playthrough plus the balance bot.\n- **Least helpful:** the data-validation suite.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** deterministic headless play via `game.advance`, and the Humanoid rigs.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** the font lacks controller glyphs and punctuation; `game.go()` before boot is overwritten; `game.every` timers die when the scene changes.\n- **Most important thing built myself:** the hex board, UI kit, both simulations, the lockstep online layer and the audio.\n- **Hardest part:** fitting a strategy game to a ground-plane engine.\n- **Engine changes:** none.\n- **One change I'd make:** a controller-first UI toolkit and font.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the concrete controller-first, attract and dev-mode spec.\n- **Confusing:** the plan was written for another model and date, with different file names than TASK.md.\n- **Hardest thing:** the plan's full content in one session.\n- **What I'd change:** mark optional plan parts and give a size budget.\n\nThe files are in `/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050226__x7910ab/work`:\n- `BrigantimeTheLegendOfForseasons-BrigandineTheLegendOfForsena-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-050226.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1935,"cache_read_input_tokens":443006,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1935},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b041f93-88ca-4f5d-be80-9273db22fc2d","uuid":"c1f7d3d2-ef47-4813-98b6-5cf1d73ed42f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:52:05.983Z","request_id":"req_011CghvFKoAQLL46Ba4Ecerh"}
