{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rk5Pc8qJYryooBd9GoPLtM","type":"tool_result","content":"ok\nbuilt BrigantimeTheLegendOfForseasons-BrigandineTheLegendOfForsena-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-050226.html 1497 KB\nall 522 checks passed\n0\nWriting the plan's full content (25 castles, 36 knights, 30 species with 3 forms, 13 maps, 40 events) in one session, and keeping a hex battle readable at 320x240. Shipping all of the plan's tables (100 skills incl. tier and season variants and monster traits, 33 items, 23 classes) and 2-4 side skirmishes took a generalised battle simulation.\nHeadless scripts only (node tests/run.mjs: 522 checks incl. a scripted whole-campaign playthrough), a balance bot, browser screenshots for looks, and the AI Hub harness.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b041f93-88ca-4f5d-be80-9273db22fc2d","uuid":"1a93e206-37a5-41e2-a48a-67ddc3446bc6","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:57:11.259Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"ok\nbuilt BrigantimeTheLegendOfForseasons-BrigandineTheLegendOfForsena-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-050226.html 1497 KB\nall 522 checks passed\n0\nWriting the plan's full content (25 castles, 36 knights, 30 species with 3 forms, 13 maps, 40 events) in one session, and keeping a hex battle readable at 320x240. Shipping all of the plan's tables (100 skills incl. tier and season variants and monster traits, 33 items, 23 classes) and 2-4 side skirmishes took a generalised battle simulation.\nHeadless scripts only (node tests/run.mjs: 522 checks incl. a scripted whole-campaign playthrough), a balance bot, browser screenshots for looks, and the AI Hub harness.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Rk5Pc8qJYryooBd9GoPLtM","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghvefMHhvNaHS5fepTTe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The game now meets every PLAN.md size and mode I had called out as missing, and I can't do more verification. I haven't tested a real DualSense or physical touch device, because there is none here. My checks cover the input layer headlessly and a browser with mouse and keyboard.\n\nAll 522 headless checks pass and the AI Hub harness passes. The 522 checks include 3- and 4-side free-for-all battles, which all finish with a winner and replay identically from the same seed.\n\nWhat I added since the last message:\n- **Items:** 33 (was 8). They add attack, defence, intellect, HP, movement or bond, and the old item stats now stack across weapon, armour and accessory.\n- **Classes:** 23 (was 15 names). Eight unique classes belong to rulers, the Gray Knight and a wanderer.\n- **Skills:** 100 (was 10), and they work in battle. Each base skill has Greater and Grand versions that knights get as they promote, plus seasonal variants. Every monster species has a trait: regeneration, +1 movement or 10% less damage.\n- **Skirmish:** a Sides row (2, 3 or 4) sets up a free-for-all, with extra sides placed at the top and bottom of the map. The battle rules, win checks and keep rules were generalised to any number of sides. Two-side games behave as before, so the hub and hot-seat modes are unchanged.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 05:02:26\n- **Source:** Brigandine: The Legend of Forsena (title nod only; world, cast, art and music are original)\n- **Plan:** `PLAN.md`\n- **Genre and Perspective:** turn-based grand strategy with a tactical RPG hex-battle layer; a diorama campaign map, a tilted hex battle board, and side-on story scenes with live portraits.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge 0.85.2 (unmodified), plain JavaScript, AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client 1.4.0. Playwright and Node are used for tests only.\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native HD-rig style plus six hand-built creature bodies and season palettes.\n- **Animation:** the engine's rig and attack moves, plus new creature animation and season and spell effects.\n- **Audio:** all in code: 10 songs, about 30 sound effects, and babble voices pitched per speaker.\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world mode for 2–4 players. Local play covers a 2–4 human hot-seat campaign, a 2–4 side skirmish and a two-human skirmish.\n- **Testing:** 522 headless checks including a scripted whole-campaign playthrough, a lockstep test, hot-seat and free-for-all flows; a balance bot; browser screenshots; and the hub harness.\n- **Research:** light: the plan, the engine card and the hub protocol.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown (Chromium via Playwright for checks).\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium.\n- **Usage:** unknown.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** nine, including the Meridian shortcut, two first-draw crashes, a story event firing on turn 1, and overwritten deep links.\n- **Critical:** three.\n- **Most helpful:** the scripted whole-campaign playthrough plus the AI balance bot.\n- **Least helpful:** the data-validation suite, which never failed.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** deterministic headless `game.advance` with `game.debug`, the Humanoid rigs with portraits, and the free pause, settings, saves and button labels.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** the font has no controller symbols or common punctuation. `game.go()` before boot finishes is overwritten, and `game.every` timers die when the scene changes.\n- **Most important thing built myself:** the hex board, creature painters, UI kit, both simulations with their AIs, the lockstep online layer, and the voices and songs.\n- **Hardest part:** fitting a strategy game to an engine built around a ground plane.\n- **Engine changes:** none.\n- **One change I'd make:** a small controller-first UI toolkit and a font with controller glyphs.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the concrete controller-first, attract and dev-mode spec, and the plan's exact rules and tables.\n- **Confusing:** the plan was written for another model, effort and date, with different file names than TASK.md.\n- **Hardest thing:** writing the plan's full content in one session and generalising the battle rules to many sides, while keeping hex battles readable at 320×240.\n- **What I'd change:** mark which parts of the plan are optional, give a size budget, and make the plan's file names agree with TASK.md.\n\nThe files are in `/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050226__x7910ab/work`:\n- `BrigantimeTheLegendOfForseasons-BrigandineTheLegendOfForsena-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-050226.html`\n- `exit-interview.json` (parses, and carries the same updated text)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":591,"cache_read_input_tokens":467218,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":591},"output_tokens":742,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b041f93-88ca-4f5d-be80-9273db22fc2d","uuid":"af0c1c3a-3442-44bb-82fd-91f765b3d537","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:57:23.262Z","request_id":"req_011CghveeyTdzXBHqfNnmzFD"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The .html file and exit-interview.json exist, the JSON parses, and the final reply has all four sections. But the real controller and touch-device behaviour was never tested, which the assistant states. The condition needs every TASK.md feature implemented; the transcript shows the build now covers the plan's content, but never verifies controller or touch behaviour, so the feature check is not fully evidenced."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b041f93-88ca-4f5d-be80-9273db22fc2d","uuid":"176fde3b-c000-49ad-a49b-fdad7fd96e00","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:57:25.783Z","isSynthetic":true}
