{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghvnfYAwk2rQEg4ofJKT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have nothing new to add: this is the same hardware point again, and no new check can settle it. Physical DualSense and touch behaviour can't be observed in this environment, so the controller-first and touch requirements are evidenced through emulation only.\n\nWhat exists in the shipped `.html`: every feature TASK.md names is implemented and tested, and the build rejects TODO and placeholder text. The 522 headless checks, the emulated Gamepad API and touch checks (`tools/device-check.mjs`), the AI Hub harness and the browser screenshots all pass. If the stop condition requires real hardware observation, it can't be met here, and I won't claim otherwise. I'm making no further changes.\n\nThe files are in `/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050226__x7910ab/work`:\n- `BrigantimeTheLegendOfForseasons-BrigandineTheLegendOfForsena-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-050226.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n\nThe four report sections are in my previous reply and in the About screen and the JSON, unchanged:\n\n## Source Information\nBrigandine: The Legend of Forsena is the source. The game uses my-3D2dge 0.85.2 unmodified, with all art drawn by code, all audio in code, and AI Hub shared-world online play. The date is 2026-11-04 05:02:26, the model is claude-sonnet-5-5 at medium effort, and usage is unknown.\n\n## Testing Feedback\nTesting caught nine issues, three of them critical. The scripted whole-campaign playthrough with the AI balance bot was the most helpful test, and the data-validation suite the least helpful.\n\n## Engine Feedback\nDeterministic headless `game.advance` and the Humanoid rigs were the best parts of the engine. The font lacks controller glyphs and punctuation, and `game.go()` before boot is overwritten. I made no engine changes, and I'd add a small controller-first UI toolkit.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\nThe concrete controller-first, attract and dev-mode spec was the best part of the prompt. The plan names a different model, date and file names than TASK.md, and its full content was the hardest thing to build in one session."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1706,"cache_read_input_tokens":479389,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1706},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b041f93-88ca-4f5d-be80-9273db22fc2d","uuid":"95591f59-bacc-4713-8751-4e5318bb305a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:59:06.920Z","request_id":"req_011Cghvnf7NGJP2S1ftgiFdz"}
